      "statement_sha256": "3b83eb37905660e3db1cc68c54e476f4ac5c450b245cec4675195f9cc2e0a95d",
      "text": "It is not the case that for all reals dIdt, P, D, kB, T with kB>0, T>0, P>=0, 0<=D<=1 one has dIdt <= maxBitRate P kB T * D, where maxBitRate P kB T = P/(kB*T*log 2); counterinstance dIdt=1, P=D=0, kB=T=1. The historical unrestricted Intelligence Bound axiom is false as written.",
      "trivial": false
    },
    "C2": {
      "kind": "conjecture",
      "label": "ASSUMED",
      "reason": "conjecture",
      "text": "For cap P D C = P*D/C with C>0, P>0, 0<dD<D: P*D/(D-dD) is the unique power restoring capacity after the loss; under a ceiling P<=Pmax it is attainable iff dD <= D*(1-P/Pmax); it diverges as dD -> D from below; and at D=0 no power restores a positive capacity (sealed statement P5.CompensationUnderCeiling, to be proved in P5-T003)."
    }
